   "created": 1794405844,
   "author": "Robert Lee-Green",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/robert-lee-green-3013a349_soon-a-screenshot-an-email-or-a-file-with-activity-7526283612778835968-mfDY",
   "text": "Soon, a screenshot, an email or a file with your name on it won't be enough to prove anything. \n\nAI can now produce a convincing version of almost anything. People are noticing, and they're starting to doubt what they see.\n\nFor businesses, that doubt shows up in very practical places. A client asking whether the work was done by your team or by a tool. An acquirer asking who actually created the IP they're paying for. A court asking you to show the evidence.\n\n\"We know what happened\" doesn't hold up when anything can be fabricated after the fact. Evidence that someone else can independently verify does. That means knowing who proposed the idea, which versions were rejected, who contributed, w",
